WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.070
This film shows how the Core Downtown
Memphis Safety Dashboard works.

2
00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:09.220
This is a self-regulated safety dashboard.

3
00:00:09.270 --> 00:00:14.220
Downtown businesses and the Downtown
public-safety team watch out for each other.

4
00:00:14.270 --> 00:00:16.380
Members report what they see.

5
00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:20.060
Officers see each report
at once, and respond.

6
00:00:20.110 --> 00:00:25.420
There are three roles: business
owner, officer, and administrator.

7
00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:28.220
This dashboard is not 911.

8
00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:32.270
If anyone is in danger, call 911 first.

9
00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:35.180
There are no passwords.

10
00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:39.580
Type your work email, and select
“Email me a sign-in link”.

11
00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:43.740
Open the email on the same
device, and select “Sign in”.

12
00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:46.940
The link works one time, for one hour.

13
00:00:46.990 --> 00:00:49.820
On a trusted device, add a passkey.

14
00:00:49.870 --> 00:00:55.310
Then sign in with Face ID,
Touch ID, or your device PIN.

15
00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:58.580
A business starts on its home page.

16
00:00:58.630 --> 00:01:02.860
Add your storefront, and one
tap pins a report to your door.

17
00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:07.553
“My reports” follows each report
that you sent, until it is resolved.

18
00:01:07.603 --> 00:01:13.260
“Nearby” shows community reports within
half a mile, from the last 48 hours.

19
00:01:13.310 --> 00:01:16.910
The side column shows your
block and the lookouts.

20
00:01:17.650 --> 00:01:22.640
You can report by voice, with a
guided form, or with a quick alert.

21
00:01:22.690 --> 00:01:25.120
Select “Report by voice”.

22
00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:29.520
An automated voice interview asks
the questions that officers need.

23
00:01:29.570 --> 00:01:31.400
Describe what you saw.

24
00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:33.840
You can interrupt at any time.

25
00:01:33.890 --> 00:01:37.600
While you talk, the report
appears on the same screen.

26
00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:40.850
Your words stay with it as a transcript.

27
00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:49.400
The guided form has five short steps:
what, where, when, who, and details.

28
00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:52.840
Select “Read aloud” to hear each question.

29
00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:57.080
Describe what people did, their
clothing, and which way they went.

30
00:01:57.130 --> 00:02:00.040
Never describe a person by race alone.

31
00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:04.760
In the last step, dictate your notes,
and select “Organize my notes”.

32
00:02:04.810 --> 00:02:08.890
It finds the category, the
people, and the vehicles.

33
00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:13.940
For something at your door right
now, select “Quick alert”.

34
00:02:13.990 --> 00:02:17.740
Select what is happening,
then “Send alert now”.

35
00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:20.060
It goes out at once.

36
00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:23.580
Voice reports and forms
end on a review page.

37
00:02:23.630 --> 00:02:29.900
The dashboard suggests a priority,
from P1, critical, to P4, low.

38
00:02:29.950 --> 00:02:33.260
A weapon or an injury makes it P1.

39
00:02:33.310 --> 00:02:38.140
Choose who sees it: your photos and
phone number stay with the officers.

40
00:02:38.190 --> 00:02:41.070
Then select “Send to officers”.

41
00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:44.120
Officers work in the Ops Center.

42
00:02:44.170 --> 00:02:47.520
A new report appears in
the queue in seconds.

43
00:02:47.570 --> 00:02:49.920
The queue sorts by priority.

44
00:02:49.970 --> 00:02:53.360
In each priority, new reports come first.

45
00:02:53.410 --> 00:02:56.720
Search, or filter by
priority and category.

46
00:02:56.770 --> 00:02:59.120
The numbers at the top show what is new,

47
00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:02.720
what is open, and the
median time to acknowledge.

48
00:03:02.770 --> 00:03:05.890
The live activity stream is on the right.

49
00:03:06.550 --> 00:03:11.780
On the map, each pin is a report,
and its color is the priority.

50
00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:16.260
A ring pulses on a new P1 or P2 report.

51
00:03:16.310 --> 00:03:20.940
Use the layers menu to show the
downtown core, the incident density,

52
00:03:20.990 --> 00:03:25.990
the last place each lookout was
seen, and the member businesses.

53
00:03:26.150 --> 00:03:28.470
Select a pin to open the report.

54
00:03:29.050 --> 00:03:32.640
To triage a report, select “Acknowledge”.

55
00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:35.000
Select “Responding” when you go.

56
00:03:35.050 --> 00:03:38.640
Then select “Resolve”,
and choose the outcome.

57
00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:41.080
The reporter sees each step.

58
00:03:41.130 --> 00:03:44.840
Change the priority, or assign
the report to yourself.

59
00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:47.720
An internal note stays with the officers.

60
00:03:47.770 --> 00:03:50.280
A public note goes to the reporter.

61
00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:54.810
To warn the block, select
BOLO, and publish a lookout.

62
00:03:55.450 --> 00:03:57.960
The dashboard also speaks.

63
00:03:58.010 --> 00:04:03.240
When a report arrives, officers hear
a chime, and a voice reads it aloud.

64
00:04:03.290 --> 00:04:06.120
Businesses hear the reports near them.

65
00:04:06.170 --> 00:04:10.120
In Settings, choose which
priorities the voice reads.

66
00:04:10.170 --> 00:04:13.560
Every report and lookout
has a “Listen” button.

67
00:04:13.610 --> 00:04:20.307
Select “Shift briefing” to hear a spoken
summary of the last 4, 12, or 24 hours.

68
00:04:20.357 --> 00:04:23.530
The Memphis Police scanner plays here too.

69
00:04:24.150 --> 00:04:28.447
The Lookout board shows people and
vehicles tied to recent reports,

70
00:04:28.497 --> 00:04:31.513
with a description and
the last place seen.

71
00:04:31.563 --> 00:04:36.180
If you see a match, select “I've
seen this”, and pin the place.

72
00:04:36.230 --> 00:04:39.700
Officers get it at once, as a P2 report.

73
00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:43.540
Do not approach, follow,
or confront anyone.

74
00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:47.110
Officers extend a lookout, or clear it.

75
00:04:47.750 --> 00:04:53.620
Insights shows the trends for
24 hours, 7 days, or 30 days.

76
00:04:53.670 --> 00:04:56.287
See the share of high-priority reports,

77
00:04:56.337 --> 00:04:59.780
and how fast officers
acknowledge and resolve them.

78
00:04:59.830 --> 00:05:05.030
A heat map shows the busiest hours,
and a list shows the hotspots.

79
00:05:05.650 --> 00:05:08.160
Administrators manage the team.

80
00:05:08.210 --> 00:05:14.080
To add an officer, type the email,
select a role, and select “Send invite”.

81
00:05:14.130 --> 00:05:17.173
The officer gets a sign-in link by email.

82
00:05:17.223 --> 00:05:20.267
Pending invites wait
for the first sign-in.

83
00:05:20.317 --> 00:05:23.970
The Businesses tab lists
the member businesses.

84
00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:26.440
Here is one day.

85
00:05:26.490 --> 00:05:29.920
An officer starts the shift
with a spoken briefing.

86
00:05:29.970 --> 00:05:33.800
A business sees something, and
reports it in two minutes.

87
00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:38.040
The officer hears it, finds
it on the map, and responds.

88
00:05:38.090 --> 00:05:43.400
Members report, officers respond,
and the community regulates itself.

89
00:05:43.450 --> 00:05:45.960
Scan the code to open the dashboard.

90
00:05:46.010 --> 00:05:50.250
If anyone is in danger, call 911 first.
